config QCC74X_UART_EDL_TRIGGER
	bool "QCC74x lightweight UART EDL trigger"
	depends on UART_INTERRUPT_DRIVEN
	depends on !SHELL
	help
	  Enables a minimal interrupt-driven UART listener that watches the
	  console UART for the string "platform reboot --edl\r\n" (23 bytes).
	  When the full string is matched the chip immediately calls
	  qc7xx_sys_reset_system_from_interface() to enter Emergency Download
	  mode, exactly as the shell "platform reboot --edl" command does.

	  Using the same trigger string as the shell command means the host
	  script (qconn_pre_flash.py) never needs to know whether the running
	  firmware has CONFIG_SHELL or CONFIG_QCC74X_UART_EDL_TRIGGER – it
	  always sends the same bytes:
	    python qconn_pre_flash.py COM7

	  IMPORTANT: This option is mutually exclusive with CONFIG_SHELL.
	  When CONFIG_SHELL=y the shell backend already owns the console UART
	  interrupt callback (uart_irq_callback_user_data_set).  Enabling
	  this option at the same time would silently override that callback,
	  breaking all shell input/output.

	  This saves approximately 30-50 KB of flash and 4-8 KB of RAM
	  compared to enabling the full shell subsystem.

	  Host side: send b"platform reboot --edl\r\n" over the serial port.
	  The same qconn_pre_flash.py script works for both shell and
	  no-shell firmware, with no extra flags needed.